{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED: exact head 556ea6c81ce2b301cd1f7a238e8da98bf98932cc on request/supersede-abandon, under implementation request #24527 and promise #24528. I examined all twelve published artifacts, reporting artifact first.\n\nAll four findings in changes-requested review #24541 (git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f11d4069c617c4bbc47b6256dcedb015438f9e21) are resolved. The MCP dispatch path now has a behavioral test; the CLI refusal names --abandon; the carry and abandon instructions include the required arguments in the correct order; and docs/reference/architecture.md@556ea6c81ce2b301cd1f7a238e8da98bf98932cc describes the adapter and surface extension, with its artifact published at this head.\n\nArchitecture: the affected layers are the application host/boundary adapter (internal/app, layer 4) and surfaces/composition (cmd/gs and cmd/gitseq-mcp, layer 7). The original head exposes the existing layer-5 Workroom supersede@1 disposition through these surfaces. This repair preserves that behavior and adds CLI advice and verification. The same-head architecture addition accurately documents the surface contract extension. The Workroom fold and kernel contracts remain unchanged.\n\nSecurity: the fixed-schema, fixed-disposition helper remains shared by signing and preflight. The new CLI hint changes only advice; it confers no authority and changes no signed payload. MCP abandonment remains subject to ordinary supersession authority and the fold's approved-head requirement. The new MCP test checks that the no-approved-head declaration is stored as supersede@1 and refused rather than quietly converted into ordinary retirement. No new signature, secret-handling, input-bound or authority defect was found. This assignment has no governing decision/request-chain bases requiring the four-fact decision-adoption path.\n\nSimplification: the headless MCP fixture is sufficient and simpler than duplicating a landing-lane fixture here. It independently catches loss of dispatch's Abandon value and loss of the signed disposition, while the CLI's approved-head test verifies successful abandonment through the same unchanged helper. No further abstraction or implementation change is needed.\n\nIndependent validation at this exact head:\n- Focused CLI abandonment and preflight tests pass (36.703s).\n- The full cmd/gitseq-mcp suite passes (56.819s).\n- TestEveryFixNamesAReasonTheFoldStillWrites passes.\n- The documentation gate passes (43.754s); diff whitespace checks pass.\n- go vet of cmd/gs, cmd/gitseq-mcp and internal/app passes; both command binaries build.\n- In a disposable clone, three compiling mutants fail their named tests: dropping MCP's dispatch Abandon value fails TestMCPSupersedeAbandonReachesTheSignedAct on its schema assertion; dropping disposition=abandoned fails that same test on the fold decision; dropping the CLI fix hint fails TestSupersedeAbandonRetiresARequestHoldingAnApprovedHead.\n\nThis is a review of the repair plus the original implementation, not a claim to have rerun the whole-repository suite at this head. The broader four-package baseline was independently verified at parent 2d3b03a96f0112bbe62027e0f365e6076c3c16b7 in #24541; this repair changes no fold, signing or preflight payload implementation. The reviewed checkout remains clean at the exact approved head.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a69704f09fba2f0633bb1afe3c759186c2241eec","binding":"assigned","head":"556ea6c81ce2b301cd1f7a238e8da98bf98932cc","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a61689ffe9c0a11eb5bb606fbcd74721bcb04bd1\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:3942429af240fadd122bdbd9ff914f014747aa1a\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a61689ffe9c0a11eb5bb606fbcd74721bcb04bd1","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}